//! A durable acknowledgement server over a byte stream: every chunk is recorded in a durable table and echoed back as
//! its acknowledgement. The echo is a stream write, released only after the tick that recorded the chunk is synced
//! (FOREIGN-PROTOCOLS §1.2), so an acknowledged chunk survives any crash.
program store version 1;

stream s: listen;

durable table seen(key: Bytes);

ack: on s.data(c, seq, b) {
    emit seen(b);
    send s.write(c, seq, [Part::Bytes(b)]);
}
